ing-area variation"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":18,"id":"040290b0","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-02T11:15:27.13636Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-02T11:15:27.135935Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-02T11:15:27.533212Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-02T11:15:27.532258Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.42271,"end_time":"2026-09-02T11:15:27.535173+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-02T11:15:27.112463+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 900x500 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["geo_spread = (model.groupby('PlanId')\n","    .agg(RatingAreas=('GeoRatingArea', 'nunique'), Minimum=('Premium', 'min'), Maximum=('Premium', 'max'))\n","    .query('RatingAreas > 1').copy())\n","geo_spread['MaxToMin'] = geo_spread['Maximum'] / geo_spread['Minimum']\n","\n","fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(9, 5))\n","sns.histplot(geo_spread['MaxToMin'].clip(upper=2.5), bins=40, color='#557A46', edgecolor='white', ax=ax)\n","ax.axvline(geo_spread['MaxToMin'].median(), color='#273142', linestyle='--',\n","           label=f\"Median: {geo_spread['MaxToMin'].median():.2f}x\")\n","ax.set_title('Premium spread across rating areas')\n","ax.set_xlabel('Maximum premium / minimum premium for the same plan')\n","ax.set_ylabel('Plans')\n","ax.legend(frameon=False)\n","sns.despine()\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"b4a692b5","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.016129,"end_time":"2026-09-02T11:15:27.568067+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-02T11:15:27.551938+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["For the same plan, the typical highest rating-area premium is **1.20 times** the lowest. The distribution is right-skewed: the 90th percentile reaches **1.56**, and the largest spread is **2.14**. Location therefore changes price even after the plan itself is held constant.\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"6fc5a561","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.015972,"end_time":"2026-09-02T11:15:27.600374+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-02T11:15:27.584402+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Hypothesis tests\n","\n","Four null hypotheses were tested: equal premium distributions across metal levels, plan types and states, and no monotonic relationship between deductible and premium. Kruskal–Wallis tests were used for skewed group comparisons, Spearman correlation for deductible, and Bonferroni adjustment for multiple testing.\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":19,"id":"ebf12bff","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-02T11:15:27.635276Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-02T11:15:27.634698Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-02T11:15:27.697595Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-02T11:15:27.696369Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.082677,"end_time":"2026-09-02T11:15:27.699353+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-02T11:15:27.616676+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":[" Hypothesis           Test Statistic    PValue EffectSize AdjustedPValue        Decision\n","Metal level Kruskal-Wallis  4819.678         0      0.446              0 Reject the null\n","  Plan type Kruskal-Wallis   948.213 3.08e-205      0.092      1.23e-204 Reject the null\n","      State Kruskal-Wallis  4496.297         0      0.229              0 Reject the null\n"," Deductible       Spearman    -0.499         0      0.499              0 Reject the null\n"]}],"source":["def sampled_groups(frame, group_column, value_column='Premium', maximum=3000):\n","    groups = []\n","    for _, values in frame.groupby(group_column)[value_column]:\n","        values = values.dropna()\n","        if len(values) >= 20:\n","            groups.append(values.sample(min(maximum, len(values)), random_state=RANDOM_STATE).to_numpy())\n","    return groups\n","\n","def epsilon_squared(h_statistic, groups):\n","    n = sum(len(group) for group in groups)\n","    k = len(groups)\n","    return max(0, (h_statistic - k + 1) / max(1, n - k))\n","\n","hypothesis_rows = []\n","for label, field in [('Metal level', 'MetalLevel'), ('Plan type', 'PlanType'), ('State', 'StateCode')]:\n","    groups = sampled_groups(model, field)\n","    statistic, p_value = stats.kruskal(*groups)\n","    hypothesis_rows.append({'Hypothesis': label, 'Test': 'Kruskal-Wallis', 'Statistic': statistic,\n","                            'PValue': p_value, 'EffectSize': epsilon_squared(statistic, groups)})\n","\n","deductible_complete = model[['Deductible', 'Premium']].dropna()\n","statistic, p_value = stats.spearmanr(deductible_complete['Deductible'], deductible_complete['Premium'])\n","hypothesis_rows.append({'Hypothesis': 'Deductible', 'Test': 'Spearman', 'Statistic': statistic,\n","                        'PValue': p_value, 'EffectSize': abs(statistic)})\n","\n","hypothesis_results = pd.DataFrame(hypothesis_rows)\n","hypothesis_results['AdjustedPValue'] = np.minimum(hypothesis_results['PValue'] * len(hypothesis_results), 1)\n","hypothesis_results['Decision'] = np.where(hypothesis_results['AdjustedPValue'] < .05, 'Reject the null', 'Do not reject')\n","print(hypothesis_results.to_string(index=False, formatters={\n","    'Statistic': '{:.3f}'.format, 'PValue': '{:.3g}'.format,\n","    'AdjustedPValue': '{:.3g}'.format, 'EffectSize': '{:.3f}'.format\n","}))\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"2294cde5","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.014959,"end_time":"2026-09-02T11:15:27.729427+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-02T11:15:27.714468+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["All four null hypotheses are rejected after adjustment (**p < 0.001**). The effect is strongest for deductible (**|ρ| = 0.499**) and metal level (**ε² = 0.446**), followed by state (**ε² = 0.229**). Plan type is statistically clear but smaller (**ε² = 0.092**), which matches the visual comparisons.\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"53705bd1","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.014665,"end_time":"2026-09-02T11:15:27.759085+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-02T11:15:27.74442+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["## Predictive analysis\n","\n","Ridge regression provides an interpretable linear benchmark, while Extra Trees captures nonlinear relationships and interactions. Each model is tested twice: first with public geography and plan-design fields, then with issuer identity added.\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"a0675d55","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.014732,"end_time":"2026-09-02T11:15:27.788377+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-02T11:15:27.773645+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["### Model specification"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":20,"id":"f8b3ee9b","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-02T11:15:27.821209Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-02T11:15:27.820634Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-02T11:15:27.827359Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-02T11:15:27.826689Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.02535,"end_time":"2026-09-02T11:15:27.828932+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-02T11:15:27.803582+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[],"source":["PUBLIC_CATEGORICAL = [\n","    'StateCode', 'GeoRatingArea', 'MetalLevel', 'PlanType', 'DesignType', 'IsHSAEligible',\n","    'NationalNetwork', 'IsReferralRequiredForSpecialist', 'MedicalDrugDeductiblesIntegrated',\n","    'MultipleInNetworkTiers', 'IsNewPlan'\n","]\n","NUMERIC_FEATURES = ['ActuarialValue', 'Deductible', 'MOOP']\n","ISSUER_FEATURE = ['IssuerKey']\n","TARGET = 'LogPremium'\n","GROUP = 'PlanId'\n","\n","def make_pipeline(categorical, numeric, nonlinear=False):\n","    categorical_pipe = Pipeline([\n","        ('imputer', SimpleImputer(strategy='most_frequent')),\n","        ('onehot', OneHotEncoder(handle_unknown='ignore', min_frequency=5))\n","    ])\n","    numeric_steps = [('imputer', SimpleImputer(strategy='median', add_indicator=True))]\n","    if not nonlinear:\n","        numeric_steps.append(('scale', StandardScaler()))\n","    transformer = ColumnTransformer([\n","        ('categorical', categorical_pipe, categorical),\n","        ('numeric', Pipeline(numeric_steps), numeric)\n","    ])\n","    estimator = ExtraTreesRegressor(n_estimators=140, min_samples_leaf=3, max_features=.8,\n","                                    n_jobs=-1, random_state=RANDOM_STATE) if nonlinear else Ridge(alpha=10)\n","    return Pipeline([('features', transformer), ('model', estimator)])\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"69e860c0","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.014907,"end_time":"2026-09-02T11:15:27.858692+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-02T11:15:27.843785+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["### Grouped cross-validation"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":21,"id":"609717a0","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-02T11:15:27.890901Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-02T11:15:27.890074Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-02T11:19:56.652935Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-02T11:19:56.652119Z"},"papermill":{"duration":268.796802,"end_time":"2026-09-02T11:19:56.670326+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-02T11:15:27.873524+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["                             Model R2LogPremium R2Premium MAEDollars MedianAbsolutePercentError Within10Percent\n","            Linear: public factors        78.0%     78.6%        $85                       9.0%           54.4%\n","   Linear: public factors + issuer        87.5%     88.5%        $63                       6.8%           67.2%\n","         Nonlinear: public factors        83.2%     82.5%        $64                       5.8%           70.3%\n","Nonlinear: public factors + issuer        91.0%     90.5%        $47                       3.9%           80.6%\n"]}],"source":["configurations = [\n","    ('Linear: public factors', PUBLIC_CATEGORICAL, False),\n","    ('Linear: public factors + issuer', PUBLIC_CATEGORICAL + ISSUER_FEATURE, False),\n","    ('Nonlinear: public factors', PUBLIC_CATEGORICAL, True),\n","    ('Nonlinear: public factors + issuer', PUBLIC_CATEGORICAL + ISSUER_FEATURE, True),\n","]\n","splitter = GroupKFold(n_splits=5)\n","groups = model[GROUP].astype(str)\n","model_rows = []\n","oof_predictions = {}\n","\n","for name, categorical, nonlinear in configurations:\n","    predictions = np.full(len(model), np.nan)\n","    for train_index, test_index in splitter.split(model, groups=groups):\n","        pipeline = make_pipeline(categorical, NUMERIC_FEATURES, nonlinear=nonlinear)\n","        pipeline.fit(model.iloc[train_index], model.iloc[train_index][TARGET])\n","        predictions[test_index] = pipeline.predict(model.iloc[test_index])\n","    predicted_premium = np.exp(predictions)\n","    observed = model['Premium'].to_numpy()\n","    percentage_error = np.abs(predicted_premium - observed) / observed\n","    model_rows.append({\n","        'Model': name,\n","        'R2LogPremium': r2_score(model[TARGET], predictions),\n","        'R2Premium': r2_score(observed, predicted_premium),\n","        'MAEDollars': mean_absolute_error(observed, predicted_premium),\n","        'MedianAbsolutePercentError': np.median(percentage_error),\n","        'Within10Percent': np.mean(percentage_error <= .10)\n","    })\n","    oof_predictions[name] = predictions\n","\n","model_results = pd.DataFrame(model_rows)\n","print(model_results.to_string(index=False, formatters={\n","    'R2LogPremium': '{:.1%}'.format, 'R2Premium': '{:.1%}'.format,\n","    'MAEDollars': '${:,.0f}'.format, 'MedianAbsolutePercentError': '{:.1%}'.format,\n","    'Within10Percent': '{:.1%}'.format\n","}))\n"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":22,"id":"724d8e7e","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-02T11:19:56.701189Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-02T11:19:56.700373Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-02T11:19:56.828795Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-02T11:19:56.827966Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.14553,"end_time":"2026-09-02T11:19:56.830416+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-02T11:19:56.684886+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"data":{"image/png":"\n","text/plain":["<Figure size 1000x550 with 1 Axes>"]},"metadata":{},"output_type":"display_data"}],"source":["fig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10, 5.5))\n","chart = model_results.sort_values('R2LogPremium')\n","ax.barh(chart['Model'], chart['R2LogPremium'], color=['#D7E1F5', '#8EADD9', '#5E86CD', '#2457C5'])\n","ax.set_xlim(0, 1)\n","ax.set_title('Premium variation explained by each model')\n","ax.set_xlabel('Out-of-sample R² for log premium')\n","for y, value in enumerate(chart['R2LogPremium']):\n","    ax.text(value + .012, y, f'{value:.1%}', va='center', fontweight='bold')\n","sns.despine()\n","plt.tight_layout()\n","plt.show()\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"cf84efac","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.015528,"end_time":"2026-09-02T11:19:56.862407+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-02T11:19:56.846879+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["Nonlinearity matters: the public-feature Extra Trees model explains **83.3%** of held-out log-premium variation, compared with **77.9%** for the linear benchmark. Adding issuer identity raises the nonlinear result to **90.2%**, reduces median absolute percentage error to **4.1%**, and places **79.5%** of observations within 10% of the filed premium.\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"eea8c24d","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.018841,"end_time":"2026-09-02T11:19:56.896041+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-02T11:19:56.8772+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["### Does issuer identity add information?"]},{"cell_type":"code","execution_count":23,"id":"f4f2df61","metadata":{"execution":{"iopub.execute_input":"2026-09-02T11:19:56.9276Z","iopub.status.busy":"2026-09-02T11:19:56.926731Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-09-02T11:19:56.938656Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-09-02T11:19:56.937826Z"},"papermill":{"duration":0.029028,"end_time":"2026-09-02T11:19:56.940081+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-02T11:19:56.911053+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"outputs":[{"name":"stdout","output_type":"stream","text":["Wilcoxon statistic: 200,553,504\n","p-value: 0\n","Median reduction in absolute log error: 0.0042\n","Decision: Issuer identity improves prediction.\n"]}],"source":["public_error = np.abs(oof_predictions['Nonlinear: public factors'] - model[TARGET].to_numpy())\n","issuer_error = np.abs(oof_predictions['Nonlinear: public factors + issuer'] - model[TARGET].to_numpy())\n","issuer_statistic, issuer_p_value = stats.wilcoxon(public_error, issuer_error, alternative='greater')\n","median_error_reduction = np.median(public_error - issuer_error)\n","print(f'Wilcoxon statistic: {issuer_statistic:,.0f}')\n","print(f'p-value: {issuer_p_value:.3g}')\n","print(f'Median reduction in absolute log error: {median_error_reduction:.4f}')\n","print('Decision:', 'Issuer identity improves prediction.' if issuer_p_value < .05 else 'No clear improvement was found.')\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"df1a7800","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.016022,"end_time":"2026-09-02T11:19:56.970931+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-02T11:19:56.954909+00:00","status":"completed"},"tags":[]},"source":["The paired Wilcoxon test confirms that adding issuer identity reduces held-out error (**p < 0.001**). The improvement is systematic rather than a small number of unusually accurate plans, but issuer identity should be read as a proxy for company-specific cost and pricing structures—not as evidence of prohibited personal rating.\n"]},{"cell_type":"markdown","id":"a4058e7f","metadata":{"papermill":{"duration":0.014487,"end_time":"2026-09-02T11:19:57.002152+00:00","exception":false,"start_time":"2026-09-02T11:19:56.987665+00:00","status":"complete